{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QDifferentialGeometry","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceTwoTerm","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_reeb_neutron_eq_one_third_six_crossing_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_reeb_neutron_eq_one_third_six_crossing_sum","kind":"theorem","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L438-L455","doc":"**Gap 1 (Boundary 6-Crossing Cyclic Sum Bridge for Neutron `V_n³ = (B₁ B₂⁻¹)³`):**\nConnects the neutron Reeb-contracted matter trace `τ (L_n.costate ≫ L_n.state ≫ L_n.dirac.reeb)`\ndirectly to `(1 / 3)` times the 6-crossing cyclic boundary sum across the 3 periods of `V_n³`\nvia `trace_borromeanV3B_six_crossing_sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_reeb_proton_eq_one_third_six_crossing_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_reeb_proton_eq_one_third_six_crossing_sum","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L419-L436","doc":"**Gap 1 (Boundary 6-Crossing Cyclic Sum Bridge for Proton `V_p³ = (A₁ A₂⁻¹)³`):**\nConnects the proton Reeb-contracted matter trace `τ (L_p.costate ≫ L_p.state ≫ L_p.dirac.reeb)`\ndirectly to `(1 / 3)` times the 6-crossing cyclic boundary sum across the 3 periods of `V_p³`\nvia `trace_borromeanV3A_six_crossing_sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_concrete_borromean_connected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_concrete_borromean_connected","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L373-L417","doc":"**Gap 2 (Connected Fourth-Order `(q - 1)⁴` Decomposition of the Concrete Traced Lagrangian Difference):**\nUnder the hypotheses of `trace_lagrangian_diff_concrete_borromean_weight_space`, separating\nthe static `q = 1` Coulomb background `(-2 / 9) * tr(V_n³)` from the neutron matter trace\nvia `trace_QAdj_connected_diff_borromeanV3` expresses `τ L_n.lagrangian - τ L_p.lagrangian`\nas the Cartan Reeb-spin term, the static `-2/9` Coulomb term, and the reinforcing\nfourth-order connected quantum braid trace `(q - 1)⁴ (q + 1)⁴ (4 q⁴ + q² + 4) / (9 q⁶)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_concrete_borromean_weight_space","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_concrete_borromean_weight_space","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L324-L371","doc":"**Gap 2 (Parameter-Free Concrete 3-Strand Weight-Space Specialization on Borromean `V³`):**\nWhen the Reeb-spin square traces `τ (D_n.reeb ≫ D_n.reeb)` and `τ (D_p.reeb ≫ D_p.reeb)`\nare evaluated on the 3-strand neutron `(1,2)` and proton `(2,1)` weight spaces with\nCartan weights `K^{⊗3}` (`q⁻¹` on `W_n`, `q` on `W_p`) on the Borromean braid\n`V³ = (σ₁ σ₂⁻¹)³` (`borromeanV3B q`, `borromeanV3A q`), and the Reeb-contracted matter\ntraces evaluate to the adjacent pairwise charge traces `tr((Q₁₂ + Q₂₃) V³)`, the traced\nLagrangian difference `τ L_n.lagrangian - τ L_p.lagrangian` evaluates to the exact\nparameter-free rational function of `q` with zero free coupling `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.hadronicScale_strong_to_matter_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.hadronicScale_strong_to_matter_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L311-L322","doc":"**Gap 5 (Strong Reeb-Spin Square vs. Matter Reeb Scale Ratio):**\nIn `CategoricalLagrangian`, the matter Reeb term carries prefactor `1 - q⁻¹ = ħ_q`\nwhile the bosonic Reeb-spin square `D.reeb ≫ D.reeb` carries `(1 - q⁻¹)² = ħ_q²`.\nConsequently, the ratio of the `hadronicScale`-weighted matter prefactor to the\nstrong `(1 - q⁻¹)²` prefactor is `m_e / (q - 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.hadronicScale_mul_q_sq_hbar_eq_me","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.hadronicScale_mul_q_sq_hbar_eq_me","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L302-L309","doc":"**Gap 5 (Exact Lagrangian Scale Hierarchy — Electronic Calibration):**\nMultiplying `hadronicScale m_e q = m_e / (q (q - 1))` by `q² * (1 - q⁻¹)` (the `q²`\nfactor times the first-order matter Reeb prefactor `ħ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`) recovers `m_e`\nidentically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.hadronicScale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.hadronicScale","kind":"def","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L297-L300","doc":"**Hadronic energy scale `E₀(q) = m_e / (q (q - 1))`** relating the fundamental electronic\nscale `m_e` to the categorical Lagrangian `ħ_q = 1 - q⁻¹` hierarchy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_nucleon_splitting_with_coulomb_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_nucleon_splitting_with_coulomb_gap","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L245-L282","doc":"**Combined Two-Term Nucleon Traced Lagrangian Splitting Theorem over `ℚ`**:\nUnder the shared 3-strand spatial closure hypotheses (`hQinv`, `hNabla`, `hCross`)\nand the pairwise Coulomb specialization (`hHoriz`, `hNeutronCoulomb`, `hProtonCoulomb`),\nthe total traced Lagrangian difference `τ L_n.lagrangian - τ L_p.lagrangian` equals\nthe positive-weighted Reeb-spin square trace difference minus `(1 - q⁻¹) * (k / 3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_diff_coulomb_specialization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_diff_coulomb_specialization","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L207-L243","doc":"**Bridge from the fermionic matter trace difference to the pairwise quark Coulomb gap**\n(`QOU.MassTheory.NeutronProtonEMSign.em_gap_eq`):\nOver `ℚ`, when the horizontal matter traces of neutron (`L_n`) and proton (`L_p`)\nagree and their Reeb-contracted matter traces evaluate to `k` times the pairwise\nquark Coulomb charge factors `chargeStructure qUp qDown qDown` (`udd`) and\n`chargeStructure qUp qUp qDown` (`uud`), the fermionic matter trace difference\nevaluates to `-(1 - q⁻¹) * (k / 3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.reeb_holonomy_leftTrace_eq_functional_hol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.reeb_holonomy_leftTrace_eq_functional_hol","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L186-L205","doc":"**Bridge from Reeb-spin square `D.reeb ≫ D.reeb` to discrete boundary holonomy trace**\n(`QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massTrace_eq_functional_hol_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit`):\nwhen the Reeb-spin square endomorphism `D.reeb ≫ D.reeb` is realized via non-abelian\nStokes descent as the mass endomorphism `leftMul fh (hol fh w) ≫ massIntegrand fh` of a\nboundary transport word `w`, its categorical trace `fh.leftTrace (D.reeb ≫ D.reeb)`\nunder `fh.frobeniusForm = fh.counit` equals the Frobenius functional\n`casimir fh ≫ leftMul fh (hol fh w) ≫ fh.frobeniusForm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_shared_spatial_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_shared_spatial_closure","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L159-L184","doc":"**Two-term nucleon splitting decomposition on a shared spatial braid closure**:\nWhen two configurations `L_n L_p : CategoricalLagrangian R C fh` share the same\ndeformation parameter `qinv`, the same spatial connection `nablaEndo`, and the same\ntraced spatial-Reeb cross-coupling on the common 3-strand closure, the classical\nspatial curvature `q⁻² τ(∇²)` and cross-coupling cancel identically in\n`τ L_n.lagrangian - τ L_p.lagrangian`, leaving strictly:\n1. The `(1 - q⁻¹)²` Reeb-spin square trace difference, plus\n2. The fermionic matter trace difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_shared_dirac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_diff_shared_dirac","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L145-L157","doc":"**Shared-Dirac state difference cancellation**: when two matter configurations\n`L_n L_p : CategoricalLagrangian R C fh` share the exact same bosonic Dirac operator\n(`L_n.dirac = L_p.dirac`), the bosonic trace `τ (D.dirac ≫ D.dirac)` cancels identically\nin `τ L_n.lagrangian - τ L_p.lagrangian`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_two_term_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_matter_two_term_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L135-L143","doc":"**Two-term traced matter expansion** under an `R`-linear trace functional\n`τ : (fh.obj ⟶ fh.obj) →ₗ[R] R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_dirac_sq_three_term_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_dirac_sq_three_term_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L124-L133","doc":"**Three-term traced `q`-Laplacian expansion** under an `R`-linear trace functional\n`τ : (fh.obj ⟶ fh.obj) →ₗ[R] R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_two_term_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.trace_lagrangian_two_term_split","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L116-L122","doc":"**Two-term trace decomposition of `L.lagrangian`** under any `R`-linear trace functional\n`τ : (fh.obj ⟶ fh.obj) →ₗ[R] R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lagrangian_five_term_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lagrangian_five_term_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L104-L114","doc":"**Full five-term expansion of `L.lagrangian : fh.obj ⟶ fh.obj`** in an `R`-linear\npreadditive monoidal category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.matter_term_two_term_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.matter_term_two_term_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L95-L102","doc":"**Two-term expansion of the fermionic matter coupling `L.costate ≫ L.state ≫ L.dirac.dirac`**\nin `fh.obj ⟶ fh.obj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.dirac_sq_three_term_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.dirac_sq_three_term_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L84-L93","doc":"**Three-term `q`-Laplacian expansion of `D.dirac ≫ D.dirac`** in `fh.obj ⟶ fh.obj`.\nGroups the middle cross-terms `(D.nablaEndo ≫ D.reeb + D.reeb ≫ D.nablaEndo)` under\nthe shared coefficient `D.qinv * (1 - D.qinv)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.dirac_sq_four_term_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.dirac_sq_four_term_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/CategoricalLagrangianTwoTermBridge.lean#L72-L82","doc":"**Four-term ungrouped bilinear expansion of `D.dirac ≫ D.dirac`** in `fh.obj ⟶ fh.obj`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}